Business Requirements Document (BRD)
Project SutraSparsh: Bhashini Localization & Voice Intelligence Module
1. Executive Summary
SutraSparsh is a multilingual text-to-speech (TTS) and recitation platform. To democratize accessibility and provide culturally nuanced, regional language synthesis, SutraSparsh requires seamless integration with India’s National Language Translation Mission (NLTM) infrastructure—Bhashini. This document outlines the business objectives, scope, and strategic value of configuring Bhashini’s Udyat and Inference pipelines into the SutraSparsh ecosystem.
2. Business Objectives
* Multilingual Expansion: Enable real-time, high-fidelity Indian language text-to-speech and translation capabilities across scheduled regional dialects.
* National Compliance & Ecosystem Alignment: Leverage government-backed open-source AI infrastructure to drastically reduce third-party API licensing costs while maintaining data sovereignty and localization standards.
* Enhanced User Engagement: Provide localized audio rendering for community-driven content sharing, scripture/text recitations, and educational modules.
3. Scope of Work
* In-Scope:
   * Secure environment variable configuration (VITE_BHASHINI_USER_ID, VITE_BHASHINI_UDYAT_KEY, VITE_BHASHINI_INFERENCE_KEY) within the frontend build system.
   * Integration of Bhashini authentication middleware and pipeline token exchange.
   * Implementation of client-side error handling, fallback mechanisms, and API rate-limiting guardrails.
* Out-of-Scope:
   * Custom model training or fine-tuning of Bhashini base models (utilizing pre-existing endpoints).
   * Backend infrastructure migration away from existing hosting providers.
4. Stakeholders & Success Metrics
* Key Stakeholders: Product Engineering, Project Management, Quality Assurance.
* Success Metrics:
   * Successful token authentication and zero unauthorized key leakage in client bundles.
   * Sub-1.5 second latency for initial audio stream generation on standard broadband/mobile networks.
   * Support for at least 10 major scheduled Indian languages within the first release cycle.
