	2. Functional Modules & User Stories
FR-01: Secure Credential Initialization & Auth Handshake
* Description: Upon application boot, the client-side module must initialize headers using the configured environment variables.
* Requirements:
   * The application must construct the authorization payload incorporating VITE_BHASHINI_USER_ID and VITE_BHASHINI_UDYAT_KEY.
   * The inference requests must append VITE_BHASHINI_INFERENCE_KEY in the designated header (e.g., ulcaApiKey or Authorization depending on the Bhashini pipeline spec).
FR-02: Pipeline Compute Service Integration (TTS / Translation)
* Description: Users inputting text in SutraSparsh can trigger text-to-speech synthesis or text translation.
* Requirements:
   * Input Validation: The UI must accept text strings and validate target language codes (ISO 639-1 / Bhashini standard language identifiers).
   * Payload Construction: The client must format requests matching Bhashini’s ULCA (Open Language Collection Architecture) pipeline specifications, passing the inference key for compute endpoint access.
   * Response Handling: Audio buffers received from Bhashini must be piped into an HTML5 audio element or Web Audio API context for immediate playback and optional caching.
FR-03: Error Handling & Graceful Fallbacks
* Description: Protect the user experience against network failures, expired tokens, or rate limits.
* Requirements:
   * If a Bhashini endpoint returns a 401 or 403 error, log the incident securely and display a user-friendly toast notification ("Language service temporarily unavailable").
   * Implement exponential backoff retry logic (maximum 3 retries) for transient network timeouts (504/502).
3. Non-Functional Requirements
* Security: Ensure VITE_ prefixed variables are handled properly in Vite build pipelines so that secret inference keys are scoped securely or routed through a proxy server if strict zero-exposure policies are mandated for production deployments.
* Performance: Audio chunk streaming should initialize playback within 1,500ms of user trigger.
* Accessibility: Audio controls generated from Bhashini TTS output must include appropriate ARIA labels for screen readers.
